From 026aae9643e3ae356640ae1077d203902bcf33f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mehedi <growwithmh@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 07:45:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Redesign Build Board UI with GrowwithMH cream theme
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The app was never dark — it carried a prefers-color-scheme block, so any
phone in dark mode rendered the whole product dark. A cream brand identity
means committing to one look, so both dark blocks are gone and the root is
pinned to color-scheme: light.

Design system
- One token set: cream surfaces, GrowwithMH navy ink, warm borders, a
  radius and shadow scale, and semantic state colours.
- The brand aqua (#2BAFA6) only reaches 2.7:1 on white, so it carries
  decoration — progress, swatches, rails — while --accent (#0F6F69) is the
  AA-safe teal used for anything readable or filled. Muted ink is never
  lighter than 4.7:1 on cream.

Layout
- Header: compact sticky bar, navy identity, tabs that read as selected by
  weight and underline as well as colour.
- The floating bottom account pill is gone. Account controls sit inline in
  the header on desktop and inside a sheet under the avatar on mobile,
  which is also where My work now lives on small screens.
- Inventory compacted to a headline plus a two-up breakdown.
- Filters read as filters; the mobile status rail is a segmented control
  whose four stages fit a 360px screen.
- Empty states say what belongs in the stage rather than that it is empty.
- FAB clears the safe area and the toast no longer shares its lane.
- Authentication gets the brand lockup and the same cream system.

No change to Supabase behaviour, auth, tenancy, RLS, invitations, realtime,
task logic, report calculations or the schema.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
